{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c42b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07acf-3bc7-7560-9750-c8ccacf23655"},"sequence":112,"recorded_at":1780531400000219,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"27563600-d9a6-4d0a-816f-45ea321ea580","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"27563600-d9a6-4d0a-816f-45ea321ea580","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"27563600-d9a6-4d0a-816f-45ea321ea580"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"0ab75a51-283a-4969-bf17-46a57c395476"},"task_id":"0ab75a51-283a-4969-bf17-46a57c395476","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"0ab75a51-283a-4969-bf17-46a57c395476","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-6-1\",\n  \"command\": \"task-board q --help 2>&1 | head -50; echo '==='; task-board worktree --help 2>&1 | head -60\",\n  \"description\": \"Inspect query and worktree commands\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"Execute queries against the board using a compact DSL.\\n\\nOperations:\\n  get(ID)              Get a single element by ID\\n  activity(ID, ...)    Read bounded, cursor-paginated element activity\\n  list(filters...)     List elements with filters\\n  count(filters...)    Count elements matching filters\\n  summary()            Board overview (counts + active/blocked)\\n  plan(scope?)         Execution phases; scope=[ID,ID,...] plans the union of subtrees\\n  agents(stale=N?)     Agent dashboard\\n  models(agent?)       Available models for spawn\\n  project_config()     Full active project board runtime config (always local)\\n  project_config(view=spawn-preflight, role=ROLE, agent=PROVIDER?)\\n                       Narrow effective child-spawn policy for one target\\n  provider_limits()    Machine-scoped provider rate-limit state (always local)\\n  provider_limits(identity=KEY|all_identities=true)\\n                       Report one indexed provider identity, or every one\\n  whoami()             Current remote URL and active user (always local)\\n  schema()             Introspect the full operations/fields/presets contract\\n  schema(operation=NAME|mutation=NAME)\\n                       Return only one typed operation or mutation signature\\n\\nField projection:\\n  { id status assignee }     Select specific fields\\n  { overview }               Use a base preset (minimal, default, overview, full, progress, planning)\\n  { observability-task }     Use project observability presets (project, epic, story, task)\\n  (omitted)                  Defaults to { id name status }\\n\\nBatching:\\n  Separate multiple queries with semicolons; results preserve source order\\n\\nSpawn policy projection:\\n  Full project_config reports the effective spawn-policy-v2/v3 contract,\\n  authority, normalized provider and role-effective policy, and exact config\\n  provenance. V2 additionally reports its frozen compatibility snapshot and a\\n  copy-ready v3 migration object; this is read-only evidence and never edits\\n  task-board.config.json. Spawn-preflight returns only the selected role policy\\n  and its actionable migration warning.\\n\\nOutput format:\\n  --format json       Standard JSON (default)\\n  --format compact    Compact tabular output (~40% fewer tokens)\\n                      plan() switches to the super-compact planning shape:\\n                      flat waves of IDs, one-line critical path, id->status map\\n\\nExamples:\\n  task-board q 'schema()'\\n  task-board q 'get(TASK-260211-abc) { id status assignee }'\\n  task-board q 'activity(TASK-260211-abc, limit=25, order=descending, view=effective)'\\n  task-board q 'list(type=task, status=development) { overview }'\\n===\\nInspect and repair the Story-scoped Git workspaces that repository-mutating\\nspawns run in.\\n\\nEach Story gets one managed worktree under .temp/<STORY-ID>/worktree on a\\nshort-lived task-board/story/<STORY-ID> branch forked from trunk. Trunk is\\nspawn.worktree_isolation.integration_base_branch when configured, and otherwise\\nresolves from refs/remotes/origin/HEAD and then the current branch.\\n\\nThese commands require a local authoritative board. On a remote board they\\nrefuse with worktree_isolation_requires_local_board and do nothing else.\\n\\nUsage:\\n  task-board worktree [command]\\n\\nAvailable Commands:\\n  abort                 Stop using a Story workspace, preserving its work by default\\n  checkpoint            Commit an accepted leaf onto its Story branch while preserving integrating\\n  gc                    Release Story leases whose holding runs are provably terminal\\n  integrate             Land an accepted Story candidate on trunk and commit its board state\\n  invalidate-acceptance Release an element whose acceptance §6.2 already invalidated back to rework\\n  repair                Re-materialize a recorded workspace whose worktree is missing\\n  status                Report managed Story workspaces and what blocks their cleanup\\n  transaction           Inspect and dispose of a refused or abandoned integration transaction\\n\\nFlags:\\n  -h, --help   help for worktree\\n\\nGlobal Flags:\\n      --board-dir string         Path to the board directory (overrides TASK_BOARD_DIR and config local.board_dir) (default \\\".task-board\\\")\\n      --context-profile string   Agent context profile override: full or lite\\n      --insecure                 Skip TLS certificate verification (for self-signed certs)\\n      --json                     Output in JSON format\\n      --no-update-check          Disable automatic update check\\n      --remote string            Remote board server URL (overrides TASK_BOARD_REMOTE)\\n      --remote-board string      Remote board ID (overrides TASK_BOARD_ID)\\n\\nUse \\\"task-board worktree [command] --help\\\" for more information about a command.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 4681,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1171,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
